From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HourlySword <hourlysword.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 21:21:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] FunKey S: the game's loop on the console (screen, buttons,
 sound, power-off)

rt/funkey.cpp (ISAAC_FUNKEY builds): main.cpp's play loop on one thread, 30 ticks a second on a fixed clock,
pictures skipped (never the logic) when behind; /dev/fb0 in RGB565 with a pan per picture; the button daemon's
keys mapped to the game's (Menu twice quits); FunKey-OS's power-off signal handled on a thread of its own, the save
written before powering off; the notification overlay for messages; a speed and memory line every 5 s. Test hooks:
ISAAC_FUNKEY_SCRIPT (a headless test script played with the real loop), ISAAC_FUNKEY_MEMLOG, ISAAC_HOME.

Sound: the FunKey's speaker is the right channel only, so the mix goes there as (L+R)/2.

Memory: lossless bitmaps over 1024 pixels a side are decoded shrunk (box-averaged by a power of 2, in strips; the
Eternal Edition's 3000x3000 light becomes 750x750), the fill matrix scaled to match: startup peak 92 MB -> 27 MB.
Decoded SWF bitmaps trimmed to 4 MB. Still graphics over 1.5x the canvas's area rasterized at their transform.
